2b. the OA is a design for the CUBE. Is it one for the sphere?
--------------------------------------------------------------
  along a coordinate axis the OA's 4th moment is 1/d^2, not 3/(d(d+2)) ok   axis 1.5259e-05  vs sphere 4.5422e-05  ratio 0.3359
  the isotropic probe is rotation-invariant, so it cannot see alignment ok   unrotated 7.550e-04  rotated 7.772e-04 — agree, as they must
  probed along the AXES, the unrotated OA is badly wrong at degree 4 ok   axis-probe 1.5259e-05 == 1/d^2, which is 0.336x the spherical value
  probed along RANDOM directions the same points are near-exact ok   7.550e-04 relative — -880x closer than the axis probe

